flowchart TB
  accTitle: Where an extension reaches
  accDescr: An extension folder holds skills, commands and agent profiles, modules without a connector block, and modules with one. Skills, commands and agent profiles go to your Claude Code and OpenCode sessions. A module without a connector block is always on: its tools and hooks go to your sessions and to the workers you start from them, and to the workers the clone starts only where the module is marked as served to workers. A module with a connector block does the same only while its switch on Set up is on, and then also gives clone turns the tools it declares for them. A worker can call a tool only when its profile names it.

  ext["Extension folder"]:::start
  files["Skills, commands, agent profiles"]
  plain["Module"]
  conn["Module with a connector block"]
  gate["Set up switch on"]:::conditional

  ext --> files
  ext --> plain
  ext --> conn
  conn --> gate

  subgraph who["Who gets it"]
    direction LR
    own["Your sessions"]
    mine["Workers you start"]
    cw["Workers the clone starts"]:::conditional
    turn["Clone turns"]:::conditional
  end

  files --> own
  plain --> own
  plain --> mine
  plain -.-> cw
  gate --> own
  gate --> mine
  gate -.-> cw
  gate -.-> turn

  classDef start fill:#ffcf4a,stroke:#1f1b16,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1f1b16,font-weight:bold
  classDef conditional fill:#ffffff,stroke:#1f1b16,stroke-width:1.5px,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#1f1b16
